  "_note": "RECONSTRUCTED, not a single verbatim Power BI export. \"Classic 2018\" is confirmed via the installed Power BI Desktop app's own minified code (desktop.min.js: S=\"CY18SU07\") to correspond to the file BaseThemes/CY18SU07.json, found inside the Power BI Desktop install at bin/WebView2Resources/minerva/sharedresources/BaseThemes/. That file and its predecessors (CY17SU10, CY17SU12, CY18SU04) are DELTA files -- each declares only \"name\" and \"visualStyles\", cumulative on top of the prior file in the chain, in the same versioned order the app itself uses (see desktop.min.js M={CY17SU10:...,CY17SU12:...,CY18SU04:...,CY18SU07:...}). This file is those four deltas deep-merged in chronological order (object keys merge recursively; arrays/primitives from the later file replace the earlier one wholesale, matching how a visualStyles group is a full array, never spliced). None of the four declare root-level colours or textClasses at all, so those are borrowed from CY19SU06.json (the next file in the same folder, chronologically) -- verified stable (byte-identical) across every file from CY19SU06 through CY25SU10, so they were already in effect, unchanged, at CY18SU07's time too, just not redeclared in that delta. Classic 2026 (verbatim, no reconstruction needed) is at themes/base/classic2026.json, sourced the same way -- confirmed via desktop.min.js: w=\"CY26SU07\"."
